<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Royal Hungary</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">from 1526</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Royal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> was the part of the medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a> ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> kings after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mohacs">Battle of Mohács</a> in 1526, consisting of the northern and western lands. With its capital and coronation city at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bratislava">Pressburg</a> (Bratislava), it formed a frontier against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-hungary">Ottoman Hungary</a> and the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a> until the reconquest of the late seventeenth century reunited most of the kingdom under Habsburg rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/royal-hungary.jpg" alt="Royal Hungary" width="320" height="305" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: WikiEditor2004 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Central_europe_1572.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
